<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Arnotts seeks share trading halt.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Arnotts seeks share trading halt.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biscuit maker Arnotts Ltd said on Friday it had requested a halt in the trading of the company's shares pending an announcement to the Australian Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Police in the Queensland state capital of Brisbane said earlier this morning that the company was the subject of a poison scare and they were attempting to track down the extortionists.  </p>
<p>Arnotts shares closed five cents up at A$8.75 on Thursday. On Friday, the stock was carrying a bid quote of A$8.40.</p>
<p>Queensland police said late on Thursday that an extortionist had threatened to plant the poisoned biscuits unless police involved in a murder case underwent a lie detector test.</p>
